INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'ee2ff8c8-d9b6-46a3-a13e-d97b9fdc8cab', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Nay on the motion to accept the 'Ought Not to Pass' report on LD 1134 (House Roll Call #481, 6/13/2025), which would have restricted school sports and facility participation to biological sex; a Nay on this ONTP motion is a vote to keep the restrictive bill alive, and the motion to kill it failed narrowly 73-72.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1134','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097524&chamber=H&serialnumber=481']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Ambureen Rana's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted AGAINST every MRTL-supported abortion restriction, including LD 253 (which would have barred the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception with criminal penalties), and voted to fund family-planning services (LD 143). Preserving public MaineCare funding and opposing restrictions at every stage matches chair 1 (legal, accessible, and publicly funded at all stages).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, $ctx$In an October 2024 Bangor Daily News candidate profile, Rana said investing in clean energy 'ensures that we leave a better life for our children, grandchildren, and future generations' and described supporting a shift away from fossil fuels while weighing environmental impacts, without calling for a climate emergency declaration or a hard 2030 phase-out deadline. This matches investing in clean energy while gradually reducing reliance on fossil fuels, rather than a market-only or emergency-ban approach.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://www.bangordailynews.com/tag/ambureen-rana/']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, $ctx$As primary sponsor, Rana secured House and Senate passage of LD 2116, which extends the sunset date of Maine's Low Income Housing Tax Credit (a subsidy for affordable rental housing development) from 2028 to December 31, 2036; it was signed into law as Public Law Chapter 699 in April 2026. She also sponsored LD 1522, the Maine Eviction Prevention Program, which would have provided $25 million over two years in eviction-prevention/rental assistance; it passed the House on 6/10/2025 but died in the Senate on 4/29/2026. Both actions reflect targeted subsidies and assistance for affordable housing development and at-risk tenants, not direct public housing construction, rent caps, or market deregulation.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2116','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1522','https://www.maine.gov/housedems/news/lawmakers-approve-rana-bill-incentivize-affordable-rental-housing-development']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'c9d094fe-1054-4804-bd24-f2cd6ceb748d', ct.id, $ctx$Rana was primary sponsor of LD 1259 (132nd Legislature), "An Act to Enhance Public Safety in Maine by Defining the Relationship Between Local and Federal Law Enforcement," which would have barred Maine police departments and state law enforcement agencies from contracting with U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE); it was referred to the Judiciary Committee and died in Legislative Files on 3/17/2026 without a floor vote. She also spoke at a January 24, 2026 Portland rally against a federal ICE operation, telling the crowd that immigrants in Maine communities live in fear day-to-day. Both actions support the most restrictive-on-cooperation, most protective-of-immigrants position.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1259','https://www.bangordailynews.com/2025/03/27/politics/state-politics/bangor-democrat-proposes-ban-maine-police-contracting-with-ice-agents-joam40zk0w/','https://www.mainemorningstar.com/2026/01/24/mainers-refuse-to-look-away-with-thousands-rallying-against-ice-operation/']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Amy Arata's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted FOR the MRTL-supported abortion restrictions, including LD 253 (barring the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception and reinstating criminal penalties). Narrowing legal abortion to a maternal-life-threat exception matches chair 4 (restrict abortion to cases of rape, incest, or serious threats to the mother's life).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Yea on House Roll Call #803 (4/9/2026) for LD 2162, which bans deployers of AI chatbots with human-like features or social AI companions from making them accessible to minors, mandates age verification, and authorizes Attorney General civil penalties up to $7,500 per violation. Supporting this ban on a specific high-risk AI use for a vulnerable population matches stance 4.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2162','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101203&chamber=H&serialnumber=803','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1451&item=1&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Nay on both LD 1870 (House Roll Call #708, 3/31/2026), a Climate Superfund program requiring major fossil fuel companies to pay for climate damages, and LD 2037 (House Roll Call #627), which tightened Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative emissions allowances. Opposing both government-imposed climate accountability and cap-tightening measures indicates a preference for market forces over regulation, matching stance 4.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1870','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099027&chamber=House&serialnumber=708','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280100902&chamber=H&serialnumber=627']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Nay on House Roll Call #715 (4/2/2026) against LD 2077's program of state grants to reduce mortgage rates for homebuyers. Opposing a taxpayer-funded homebuyer subsidy indicates a preference for reduced government intervention in housing affordability, matching stance 4.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2077','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101124&chamber=House&serialnumber=715']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Nay on House Roll Call #574 (6/18/2025) against LD 1971, which became law (PL ch. 517) over her opposition and bars state/local law enforcement from using resources for immigration enforcement, detaining people solely on ICE hold requests, or transferring them to ICE absent a court order or warrant. Opposing this restriction indicates support for continued proactive cooperation with federal immigration authorities, matching stance 4.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1971','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099282&chamber=H&serialnumber=574','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP1315&item=3&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='residential-zoning' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Nay on House Roll Call #534 (6/16/2025) against LD 427's statewide ban on mandatory parking-space minimums in building codes, though the bill was ultimately signed into law. Opposing removal of this local zoning tool suggests a preference for retaining municipal design/parking review rather than blanket deregulation, matching stance 2.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=427','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280096272&chamber=H&serialnumber=534']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='residential-zoning' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Nay on House Roll Call #474 (6/13/2025) against LD 229, which added three new state income tax brackets (7.52%, 7.15%, 8.2%) on income above roughly $205,000 (single)/$410,000 (joint) while raising entry thresholds for existing lower brackets. Opposing new higher brackets on top earners in favor of the existing rate structure matches stance 3.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=229','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280095865&chamber=House&serialnumber=474','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0152&item=1&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'd886838f-6e64-43d7-ab84-5a8f300055df', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Nay on House Roll Call #481 (6/13/2025), opposing acceptance of the 'Ought Not to Pass' report on LD 1134 and thereby voting to keep alive a bill that would have barred transgender girls/women from participating in female school sports or using female facilities based on sex. This vote to advance a bill requiring competition by biological sex matches stance 4.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1134','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097524&chamber=H&serialnumber=481']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Amy Kuhn's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted AGAINST every MRTL-supported abortion restriction, including LD 253 (which would have barred the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception with criminal penalties), and voted to fund family-planning services (LD 143). Preserving public MaineCare funding and opposing restrictions at every stage matches chair 1 (legal, accessible, and publicly funded at all stages).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 2162, "An Act to Regulate and Prevent Children's Access to Artificial Intelligence Chatbots with Human-like Features" (House Roll Call #803, 4/9/2026, passed as an emergency measure 104-43), which bans deployers of AI chatbots with human-like features or social AI companions from making them accessible to minors, mandates age verification, and authorizes Attorney General civil penalties. Supporting this targeted safety restriction on a specific high-risk AI use for a vulnerable population matches stance 4.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2162','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101203&chamber=H&serialnumber=803']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='childcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for LD 1955, "An Act to Increase Child Care Affordability and Early Childhood Educator Stability" (House Roll Call #634, 3/5/2026), which expands subsidies and provider support to make childcare more affordable and stabilize the childcare workforce, matching stance 2.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1955','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099161&chamber=H&serialnumber=634']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='childcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted to advance LD 1870, establishing a Climate Superfund Cost Recovery Program requiring major fossil fuel companies to pay for climate damages (House Roll Call #708, 3/31/2026; signed into law 4/16/2026), and voted for enactment of LD 2037, updating Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative (RGGI) emissions allowances (House Roll Call #627, 2/26/2026; signed as PL ch. 550). Both are incremental market/liability-based emissions tools rather than an outright fossil fuel ban, consistent with investing in clean energy while gradually reducing reliance on fossil fuels, matching stance 3.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1870','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099027&chamber=H&serialnumber=708','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280100902&chamber=H&serialnumber=627']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='healthcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 70, "An Act to Fund Free Health Clinics" (House Roll Call #601, 6/25/2025; signed as PL ch. 439), and for LD 1937, requiring hospitals and hospital-affiliated providers to offer financial assistance programs for medical care (House Roll Call #543, 6/17/2025; signed as PL ch. 488). Both measures expand assistance for people who can't afford care while leaving the private insurance system in place, matching stance 3.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=70','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280095624&chamber=H&serialnumber=601','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099115&chamber=H&serialnumber=543']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='healthcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted to advance LD 2077, providing state grants to reduce mortgage rates for homebuyers (House Roll Call #715, 4/2/2026; passed the House but died in the Senate). Supporting a targeted first-time-buyer mortgage subsidy program matches stance 3's "targeted help like subsidies for affordable projects, first-time buyer assistance."$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2077','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101124&chamber=H&serialnumber=715']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted to accept the "Ought Not to Pass" committee report on LD 1318, "An Act to Enhance Data Collection Requirements Related to Immigration Status and Asylum Seekers to Safeguard Services for Legal Residents" (House Roll Call #532, 6/16/2025, ONTP prevailed 78-70), killing a bill that would have restricted public-service eligibility based on immigration/asylum status. Opposing this services restriction indicates support for keeping public services broadly available regardless of legal status, matching stance 2.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1318','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097862&chamber=H&serialnumber=532']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 1971, "An Act to Protect Workers in This State by Clarifying the Relationship of State and Local Law Enforcement Agencies with Federal Immigration Authorities" (House Roll Call #574, 6/18/2025; signed into law as PL ch. 517), which bars state/local law enforcement from using resources for immigration enforcement, detaining people solely on ICE hold requests, or transferring people to ICE absent a court order or warrant. Also voted to accept the "Ought Not to Pass" report on LD 1656, which would have compelled greater local cooperation with federal immigration authorities (House Roll Call #540, 6/17/2025), killing that bill. Both votes reflect refusing ICE detainers and limiting local law enforcement cooperation with federal immigration authorities, matching stance 1.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1971','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099282&chamber=H&serialnumber=574','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280098509&chamber=H&serialnumber=540']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='residential-zoning' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 427, prohibiting mandatory parking space minimums in state and municipal building codes (House Roll Call #534, 6/16/2025; signed as PL ch. 374). Supporting a statewide removal of local parking-requirement mandates to ease denser housing development matches stance 4's call to "reduce parking requirements."$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=427','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280096272&chamber=H&serialnumber=534']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='residential-zoning' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='school-vouchers' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted to accept the "Ought Not to Pass" committee report on LD 1853, "An Act to Establish an Educational Tax Credit Program to Help Parents Pay for Nonpublic School Tuition and Fees" (House Roll Call #529, 6/16/2025, ONTP prevailed 77-71), killing a proposed tax-credit voucher program that would have diverted funds to private/nonpublic school tuition. Voting to reject this new voucher-like mechanism matches stance 1's opposition to diverting taxpayer money to private institutions.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1853','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280098955&chamber=H&serialnumber=529']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='school-vouchers' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 229, "An Act to Bring Fairness in Income Taxes to Maine Families," which raised income thresholds for the existing 5.8/6.75/7.15% brackets and added three new brackets up to 8.2% on income over $500,000 (single)/$1,000,000 (joint) (House Roll Call #474, 6/13/2025). This is a moderate increase targeted at higher earners while easing the burden on middle incomes, not a drastic across-the-board hike, matching stance 2.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=229','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280095865&chamber=H&serialnumber=474']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '403fb454-25fd-4c9f-9657-975715511b57', ct.id, $ctx$Voted to accept the "Ought Not to Pass" committee report on LD 1134, "An Act to Prohibit Males from Participating in Female Sports or Using Female Facilities," which would have barred transgender girls/women from participating in female school sports or using female facilities based on sex; accepting ONTP killed the ban (House Roll Call #481, 6/13/2025, prevailing 73-72). Voting to reject an outright competition ban is the clearest evidence available, matching stance 2 as the nearest pro-inclusion chair this record supports.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1134','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097524&chamber=H&serialnumber=481']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Amy Roeder's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted AGAINST every MRTL-supported abortion restriction, including LD 253 (which would have barred the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception with criminal penalties), and voted to fund family-planning services (LD 143). Preserving public MaineCare funding and opposing restrictions at every stage matches chair 1 (legal, accessible, and publicly funded at all stages).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Yea on House Roll Call 803 (4/9/2026), an emergency-enactment vote (104-43) for LD 2162, "An Act to Regulate and Prevent Children's Access to Artificial Intelligence Chatbots with Human-like Features and Social Artificial Intelligence Companions," which restricts a specific high-risk consumer AI use case for minors. This support for banning/restricting a high-risk AI application, short of a blanket pre-approval regime for all AI systems, matches the stance 4 chair.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2162','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101203&chamber=H&serialnumber=803']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='childcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Yea on House Roll Call 634 (3/5/2026) to accept the Ought-to-Pass-as-Amended report on LD 1955, "An Act to Increase Child Care Affordability and Early Childhood Educator Stability," which expands subsidies and support to lower family child care costs while stabilizing the early-childhood-educator workforce. This significant subsidy/provider-support expansion (short of a universal publicly-funded system) matches the stance 2 chair.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1955','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099161&chamber=House&serialnumber=634']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='childcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Yea on House Roll Call 708 (3/31/2026) for LD 1870, "An Act to Establish a Climate Superfund Cost Recovery Program to Impose Penalties on Climate Polluters," which was signed into law; she also supported other clean-energy expansion measures this session including LD 1966 (community solar access) and LD 2037 (Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative allowance updates). This pattern of imposing costs on polluters while expanding renewables matches the stance 2 chair (rapid transition to renewables paired with penalizing fossil-fuel-linked emissions).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1870','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099027&chamber=House&serialnumber=708']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='deportation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$On House Roll Call 540 (6/17/2025), Roeder voted Yea to accept an "Ought Not to Pass" report on LD 1656, "An Act to Facilitate Compliance with Federal Immigration Law by State and Local Government Entities" -- a Yea on this ONTP motion killed a bill that would have mandated state/local cooperation with federal immigration enforcement. She then voted Yea for enactment (Roll Call 574, 6/18/2025) of LD 1971, "An Act to Protect Workers in This State by Clarifying the Relationship of State and Local Law Enforcement Agencies with Federal Immigration Authorities," which became law without the Governor's signature. Together these votes show a consistent posture limiting state/local involvement in federal removal enforcement, matching the stance 1 chair.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1656','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280098509&chamber=H&serialnumber=540','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1971']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='deportation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Yea on House Roll Call 715 (4/2/2026) enacting-vote support for LD 2077, "An Act to Reduce the Cost of Purchasing a Home by Providing Grants to Reduce Mortgage Rates," a targeted first-time-homebuyer grant program; she also backed similar targeted-subsidy bills this session (LD 2057 rehabilitation of affordable manufactured housing, LD 1016 manufactured housing communities). This pattern of support for subsidy/grant programs rather than public housing construction or rent caps matches the stance 3 chair (targeted subsidies, first-time buyer assistance).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2077','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101124&chamber=House&serialnumber=715']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$Voted Yea twice (House Roll Call 441 on 6/11/2025 to accept the Ought-to-Pass-as-Amended report, and Roll Call 474 on enactment) for LD 229, "An Act to Bring Fairness in Income Taxes to Maine Families by Adjusting the Tax Brackets and Tax Rates." The bill passed on a near party-line vote (75-67 House) with a minority Ought-Not-To-Pass report from Republicans, indicating a bracket/rate restructuring aimed at shifting burden toward higher earners; exact bracket figures were not available in the bill-status page, so this is read as a moderate progressive adjustment rather than a drastic overhaul, matching stance 2.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=229','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280095865&chamber=House&serialnumber=441']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '74eb8c85-b789-4767-bdd1-206009b7cd11', ct.id, $ctx$On House Roll Call 481 (6/13/2025), Roeder voted Yea to accept the committee's "Ought Not to Pass" report on LD 1134, "An Act to Prohibit Males from Participating in Female Sports or Using Female Facilities" -- under Maine's ONTP convention a Yea on this motion KILLS the bill, meaning she voted against the proposed ban on transgender athletes' participation. This vote was part of a package of similar restriction bills (LD 1337, LD 233) also rejected that week. Voting to reject the only restriction proposal on the floor, with no vote found supporting any documentation or case-by-case restriction, matches the stance 1 chair (no restrictions).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1134','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097524&chamber=H&serialnumber=481']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
