INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, $ctx$Ray voted Yea on 2/26/2026 for Enactment of LD 2037, "An Act to Update the Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative Allowances," which was signed into law, supporting Maine's continued participation in the multistate RGGI carbon-cap-and-invest program. This matches investing in clean energy while gradually reducing reliance on fossil fuels.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2037','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280100902&chamber=H&serialnumber=627']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='healthcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, $ctx$Ray voted Yea on 3/30/2026 to accept the amended committee report on LD 2151, "An Act to Improve Access to Affordable Prescription Drugs in Underserved Areas," an emergency measure that passed the House before dying in the Senate at adjournment. This targeted support for prescription-drug affordability in underserved communities matches helping people who can't afford care while keeping private insurance for everyone else.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2151','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101120&chamber=H&serialnumber=701']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='healthcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, $ctx$Ray voted Yea on 6/18/2025 for Enactment of LD 1971, which bars Maine law enforcement agencies from using resources for immigration enforcement or detaining someone solely on an immigration hold request, but expressly permits transfers to federal immigration authorities when backed by a court order or criminal warrant. He also voted Yea on 6/17/2025 to kill LD 1656, a competing bill requiring proactive compliance with federal immigration enforcement.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1971','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099282&chamber=H&serialnumber=574','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280098509&chamber=H&serialnumber=540']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='residential-zoning' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, $ctx$As a member of the Transportation Committee, Ray voted Yea on 6/16/2025 on LD 427, "An Act to Prohibit Mandatory Parking Space Minimums in State and Municipal Building Codes," which was signed into law and eliminates state and municipal parking-minimum mandates. Supporting removal of parking requirements matches reducing parking requirements citywide as part of prioritizing multimodal investment.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=427','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280096272&chamber=H&serialnumber=534']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='residential-zoning' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, $ctx$Ray voted Yea on 6/13/2025 for Enactment of LD 229, "An Act to Bring Fairness in Income Taxes to Maine Families by Adjusting the Tax Brackets and Tax Rates," which added three new top income tax brackets reaching 8.2% (up from a 7.15% top rate) on higher incomes while raising the thresholds of the existing lower brackets to benefit middle-income filers. This is a moderate, graduated increase targeted at higher earners.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=229','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280095865&chamber=H&serialnumber=474','http://www.mainelegislature.org/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0152&item=1&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'bf3d8a5d-f5a6-4bfa-b144-513898d12ed5', ct.id, $ctx$Ray voted Yea on 6/13/2025 to accept the House minority report "Ought Not to Pass" on LD 868, which would have required students to participate in school athletics, restrooms and housing based on biological sex, and voted Nay against the alternative report that would have advanced it as amended -- effectively voting to kill the restrictive bill and preserve the existing policy of participation matching gender identity without added restrictions.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=868','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097110&chamber=H&serialnumber=490']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '59df0b0d-f559-4e37-8f3a-1f8ae5b09485', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '59df0b0d-f559-4e37-8f3a-1f8ae5b09485', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Dani O'Halloran's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted AGAINST every MRTL-supported abortion restriction, including LD 253 (which would have barred the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception with criminal penalties), and voted to fund family-planning services (LD 143). Preserving public MaineCare funding and opposing restrictions at every stage matches chair 1 (legal, accessible, and publicly funded at all stages).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '59df0b0d-f559-4e37-8f3a-1f8ae5b09485', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '59df0b0d-f559-4e37-8f3a-1f8ae5b09485', ct.id, $ctx$On LD 1971, "An Act to Protect Workers in This State by Clarifying the Relationship of State and Local Law Enforcement Agencies with Federal Immigration Authorities," which bars Maine state/local police from doing work whose primary purpose is federal immigration enforcement, O'Halloran publicly opposed the restriction and argued for continued cross-jurisdictional law-enforcement collaboration, consistent with favoring proactive cooperation with federal immigration authorities rather than restricting it. The bill passed the House 74-73 on June 17, 2025 and was enacted without the Governor's signature.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainemorningstar.com/2025/06/17/by-one-vote-maine-house-passes-restrictions-on-federal-immigration-enforcement/','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=1971&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '59df0b0d-f559-4e37-8f3a-1f8ae5b09485', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '59df0b0d-f559-4e37-8f3a-1f8ae5b09485', ct.id, $ctx$As a Judiciary Committee member, O'Halloran signed Report A (Ought To Pass As Amended) on LD 233, "An Act to Prohibit Biological Males from Participating in School Athletic Programs and Activities Designated for Females When State Funding Is Provided to the School," and was one of four House Democrats who crossed over to join all Republicans in a 73-70 House floor vote to pass it on June 13, 2025. She stated support for restricting girls'-team eligibility to biological sex while affirming support for the right to transition generally, matching the chair requiring competition on teams matching biological sex assigned at birth.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=233&snum=132','https://www.mainepublic.org/politics/2025-06-13/maine-house-deadlocks-on-transgender-athletes-bill','https://mainemorningstar.com/2025/06/16/though-majority-of-anti-trans-bills-rejected-maine-house-narrowly-advances-trans-girls-sports-ban/']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Daniel Ankeles's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted AGAINST every MRTL-supported abortion restriction, including LD 253 (which would have barred the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception with criminal penalties), and voted to fund family-planning services (LD 143). Preserving public MaineCare funding and opposing restrictions at every stage matches chair 1 (legal, accessible, and publicly funded at all stages).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 2162, regulating and restricting children's access to AI chatbots with human-like features and social AI companions (House Roll Call #803, 4/9/2026, passed as an emergency measure 104-43). This targeted restriction on a specific high-risk AI use case for minors aligns with requiring safety limits on high-risk AI applications.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=2162','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101203&chamber=H&serialnumber=803']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='ai-regulation' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='childcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for LD 1955, "An Act to Increase Child Care Affordability and Early Childhood Educator Stability" (House Roll Call #634, 3/5/2026), which expands subsidies and provider support to make childcare more affordable and stabilize the childcare workforce.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1955','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099161&chamber=H&serialnumber=634']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='childcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted to advance LD 1870, establishing a Climate Superfund Cost Recovery Program to impose penalties on climate polluters (House Roll Call #708, 3/31/2026; signed into law 4/16/2026), and voted for enactment of LD 2037, updating Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative (RGGI) emissions allowances (House Roll Call #627, 2/26/2026; signed as PL ch. 550). Both are incremental market/liability-based emissions tools rather than an outright fossil fuel ban, consistent with investing in clean energy while gradually reducing fossil fuel reliance.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1870','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099027&chamber=H&serialnumber=708','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280100902&chamber=H&serialnumber=627']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='healthcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 70, "An Act to Fund Free Health Clinics" (House Roll Call #601, 6/25/2025; signed as PL ch. 439), and for LD 1937, requiring hospitals and hospital-affiliated providers to offer financial assistance programs for medical care (House Roll Call #543, 6/17/2025; signed as PL ch. 488). Both measures expand assistance for people who can't afford care while leaving the private insurance system in place.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=70','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280095624&chamber=H&serialnumber=601','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099115&chamber=H&serialnumber=543']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='healthcare' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 3.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 427, prohibiting mandatory parking space minimums in state and municipal building codes (House Roll Call #534, 6/16/2025; signed as PL ch. 374), reducing a regulatory barrier to housing construction, and voted to advance LD 2077, providing grants to reduce mortgage rates for homebuyers (House Roll Call #715, 4/2/2026). Together these reflect targeted buyer assistance plus eased development rules rather than direct public housing construction or a hands-off market approach.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=427','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280096272&chamber=H&serialnumber=534','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280101124&chamber=H&serialnumber=715']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 1971, "An Act to Protect Workers in This State by Clarifying the Relationship of State and Local Law Enforcement Agencies with Federal Immigration Authorities" (House Roll Call #574, 6/18/2025; became law 1/11/2026 as Ch. 517), limiting state/local law enforcement's role in federal immigration enforcement. Also voted to accept the "Ought Not to Pass" report on LD 1656, "An Act to Facilitate Compliance with Federal Immigration Law by State and Local Government Entities," killing a bill that would have compelled greater local cooperation with federal immigration authorities (House Roll Call #540, 6/17/2025).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1971','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280099282&chamber=H&serialnumber=574','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280098509&chamber=H&serialnumber=540']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted for enactment of LD 229, "An Act to Bring Fairness in Income Taxes to Maine Families," which raises the income thresholds for the existing 5.8/6.75/7.15% brackets and adds three new brackets up to 8.2% on income over $500,000 (single)/$1,000,000 (joint) (House Roll Call #474, 6/13/2025). This is a moderate increase targeted at higher earners while easing the burden on middle incomes, not a drastic across-the-board hike.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=229','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280095865&chamber=H&serialnumber=474','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=HP0152&item=1&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='taxes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, 2.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'fb5600ed-e81a-4e9d-b3e2-9d57237349ad', ct.id, $ctx$Voted to accept the "Ought Not to Pass" committee report on LD 1134, "An Act to Prohibit Males from Participating in Female Sports or Using Female Facilities," killing the proposed ban (House Roll Call #481, 6/13/2025). Rejecting an outright competition ban is the clearest evidence available, though the record does not establish a position on any documentation requirement.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1134','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097524&chamber=H&serialnumber=481']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '18b11787-c861-4996-aba5-3b863ea33b1d', ct.id, 1.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '18b11787-c861-4996-aba5-3b863ea33b1d', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Daniel Sayre's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted AGAINST every MRTL-supported abortion restriction, including LD 253 (which would have barred the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception with criminal penalties), and voted to fund family-planning services (LD 143). Preserving public MaineCare funding and opposing restrictions at every stage matches chair 1 (legal, accessible, and publicly funded at all stages).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
