INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'e8cbe890-b3ac-44b9-baf3-d4d988b7c1cc', ct.id, $ctx$Hall voted Yea to accept the Veterans and Legal Affairs Committee's Ought Not to Pass report on LD 349 (An Act to Repeal the Laws That Allow Same-day Voter Registration), House Roll Call 154 on 5/20/2025 -- voting to reject the repeal and preserve same-day voter registration, an access-expanding position.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=349','http://www.mainelegislature.org/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280096167&chamber=H&serialnumber=154']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='voting-rights' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'cce50333-2b4e-48f0-987c-7d1b579ee691', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'cce50333-2b4e-48f0-987c-7d1b579ee691', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Reagan Paul's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted FOR the MRTL-supported abortion restrictions, including LD 253 (barring the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception and reinstating criminal penalties). Narrowing legal abortion to a maternal-life-threat exception matches chair 4 (restrict abortion to cases of rape, incest, or serious threats to the mother's life).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT 'cce50333-2b4e-48f0-987c-7d1b579ee691', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT 'cce50333-2b4e-48f0-987c-7d1b579ee691', ct.id, $ctx$In a May 2026 letter to Maine's Department of Energy Resources reported by Maine Wire, Paul requested a full accounting of the system effects costs of wind and solar generation, arguing that claims wind and solar are the cheapest generation sources do not hold up once hidden costs passed to ratepayers are counted; this reflects a preference for market-tested cost transparency over continued state-driven renewable-energy mandates and subsidies.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://www.themainewire.com/2026/05/rep-reagan-paul-requests-that-maine-doe-assess-true-hidden-costs-of-green-energy-agenda/']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, $ctx$Per the Maine Right to Life 2025 House scorecard (Richard Campbell's own recorded roll-call votes, 132nd Legislature), the representative voted FOR the MRTL-supported abortion restrictions, including LD 253 (barring the MaineCare program from covering abortion services) and LD 682 (narrowing legal abortion to a life-of-mother exception and reinstating criminal penalties). Narrowing legal abortion to a maternal-life-threat exception matches chair 4 (restrict abortion to cases of rape, incest, or serious threats to the mother's life).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainerighttolife.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/2025-132nd-House-Roll-Call.pdf','https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/display_ps.asp?LD=253&snum=132']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='abortion' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, $ctx$In a Dec. 13, 2023 op-ed on the House Republican caucus site opposing Maine's proposed Advanced Clean Cars II rule (which would have required 43% of new car sales be electric by 2027, rising to 82% by 2032), Campbell -- the House Republican lead on the Environment and Natural Resources Committee -- argued the state should not impose an EV sales mandate and that "public opinion should matter and the government should not require us to buy things we do not want or need." He said he would submit emergency legislation to repeal the rule if the Board of Environmental Protection adopted it and called for requiring legislative approval before any such rule could take effect. This opposition to a government mandate forcing a clean-energy transition, in favor of consumer/market choice, matches the stance 4 chair (letting market forces drive any transition to cleaner energy).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainehousegop.org/member_news_item/maine-should-not-move-toward-eliminating-gas-powered-vehicles/']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='climate-change' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, $ctx$As primary sponsor of H.P. 309 / L.D. 492, "An Act to Repurpose Vacant Shopping Mall and Retail Space to Mixed-use Housing and Retail" (131st Legislature, enacted 1/7/2024 as Public Law ch. 490, confirmed on the official chaptered-law PDF), Campbell created a permissive (not mandatory) municipal ordinance option allowing residential units in vacant/partially-vacant commercial and retail zones. In his own account of the bill, published on his party caucus site, he said his intent was "to encourage, not mandate, communities to think beyond present zoning and comprehensive planning, thus to accommodate today's needs cost effectively," framing the housing shortage as a supply problem best solved by removing zoning barriers for private redevelopment rather than public housing construction or rent regulation. This zoning-deregulation, private-developer-driven approach matches the stance 4 chair.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://mainehousegop.org/member_news_item/1140/','https://legislature.maine.gov/backend/App/services/getDocument.aspx?documentId=104472','https://growsmartmaine.org/blog/ld-492/']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='housing' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, $ctx$On House Roll Call No. 540 (6/17/2025, verified on the authoritative rollcall.asp page), Campbell voted Nay on the motion to accept the committee's "Ought Not to Pass" report on L.D. 1656, "An Act to Facilitate Compliance with Federal Immigration Law by State and Local Government Entities." A Nay on this ONTP motion is a vote AGAINST killing the bill, meaning Campbell voted to keep alive a measure requiring state and local government cooperation with federal immigration enforcement. This individual recorded vote matches the stance 4 chair (honoring federal immigration enforcement requests and sharing information proactively), the inverse of the position taken by colleagues who voted to kill the same bill.$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1656','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280098509&chamber=H&serialnumber=540']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='local-immigration' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_answers (politician_id, topic_id, value) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, 4.0 FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET value=EXCLUDED.value;
INSERT INTO inform.politician_context (politician_id, topic_id, reasoning, sources) SELECT '1f6fb9ae-a29b-4174-baf3-1116371c4955', ct.id, $ctx$On House Roll Call No. 481 (6/13/2025, verified on the authoritative rollcall.asp page), Campbell voted Nay on the motion to accept the committee's "Ought Not to Pass" report on L.D. 1134, "An Act to Prohibit Males from Participating in Female Sports or Using Female Facilities." Under Maine's ONTP convention a Nay vote is a vote AGAINST killing the bill, meaning Campbell voted to keep alive -- and by extension supported -- the proposed requirement that female sports/facilities eligibility be based on sex, not gender identity. This individual recorded vote matches the stance 4 chair (requiring transgender athletes to compete on teams matching their biological sex assigned at birth).$ctx$, ARRAY['https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/summary.asp?LD=1134','https://legislature.maine.gov/LawMakerWeb/rollcall.asp?ID=280097524&chamber=H&serialnumber=481']::text[] FROM inform.compass_topics ct WHERE ct.topic_key='trans-athletes' ON CONFLICT (politician_id, topic_id) DO UPDATE SET reasoning=EXCLUDED.reasoning, sources=EXCLUDED.sources;
